================================================================================
Summary — Request flow pattern (common to both runs)
================================================================================

  Phase                   Method   Endpoint
  -----                   ------   --------
  1. Dex OIDC init        GET      /dex/auth
  2. LDAP login           POST     /dex/auth/lldap/login
  3. OpenFGA check ×3     POST     /stores/{store_id}/check   (can_connect, can_use, can_provision/can_read)
  4. Session info         GET      /v1/auth/me
  5. Connection test      POST     /v1/connections:test
  6. Discovery calls      GET      /v1/compute/locations
                          GET      /v1/compute/sizes
                          GET      /v1/compute/images
                          GET      /v1/compute/storage-containers  (Nutanix only)
                          GET      /v1/compute/nodes
                          GET      /v1/compute/subnets             (before create only)
  7. Node creation        POST     /v1/compute/nodes


================================================================================
Differences between runs
================================================================================

  Aspect                 run3 (AWS)                                  run4 (Nutanix)
  ------                 -----------                                 --------------
  User                   1 session (aws-admin)                       2 sessions (ntnx-admin, ntnx-viewer)
  storage-containers     NOT called                                  Called (both sessions)
  locations              Called once                                 Called twice (ntnx-admin only)
  images                 Called twice with ?name=*Ubuntu* filter      Called twice (ntnx-admin), once (ntnx-viewer)
  sizes                  Called twice                                Called once per session
  subnets                Called once (before node create)            Called once (before node create, ntnx-admin only)
  Node creation          Yes                                         Yes (ntnx-admin only; ntnx-viewer ends at GET /nodes)
  OpenFGA check #3       can_provision:nutanix_cluster:nutanix       ntnx-admin: can_provision / ntnx-viewer: can_read
